1
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:05,000
I'm so hungry.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,333
I just want to go home and eat.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,125
Yeah.

4
00:00:07,291 --> 00:00:08,250
It's all because of sports day.

5
00:00:08,583 --> 00:00:10,541
School should be over by now.

6
00:00:11,125 --> 00:00:12,291
Well, you signed up for it.

7
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:13,750
I didn't want to.

8
00:00:14,333 --> 00:00:16,583
Mr. Chen said each class had to send two
people.

9
00:00:17,041 --> 00:00:18,083
So I was just there to make up the numbers.

10
00:00:18,875 --> 00:00:19,750
Hey, Zhu Tong.

11
00:00:20,083 --> 00:00:21,125
Why did you sign up?

12
00:00:21,375 --> 00:00:22,125
I...

13
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:23,166
Hey!

14
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:24,875
What are you doing here?

15
00:00:25,041 --> 00:00:26,166
The race is about to start.

16
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:26,541
Yes, sir.

17
00:00:27,625 --> 00:00:27,958
Yes, sir.

18
00:00:37,916 --> 00:00:39,416
Across the mountains,

19
00:00:39,416 --> 00:00:40,833
chasing the waves,

20
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:42,125
keep on running.

21
00:00:53,041 --> 00:00:54,083
Why did I sign up?

22
00:00:54,666 --> 00:00:55,708
I can't quite explain it.

23
00:00:56,208 --> 00:00:57,458
On your marks!

24
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:58,625
Whatever happens,

25
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:00,375
I want to win.

26
00:01:30,291 --> 00:01:31,125
You've been holding out on us!

27
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:32,166
You're so fast!

28
00:01:32,375 --> 00:01:33,291
Yeah, exactly!

29
00:01:33,416 --> 00:01:34,333
Nobody could catch you.

30
00:01:44,250 --> 00:01:45,083
Wait for me!

31
00:01:51,958 --> 00:01:52,791
Wait for me!

32
00:01:53,083 --> 00:01:53,958
Wait for me!

33
00:01:54,208 --> 00:01:55,000
Wait for me!

34
00:01:58,208 --> 00:02:00,000
I don't want to go to school!

35
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,208
I don't want to go today!

36
00:02:01,208 --> 00:02:01,875
Come on, hurry up!

37
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:02,708
We're going to be late.

38
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:03,458
Excuse me, coming through!

39
00:02:03,458 --> 00:02:04,333
Could you move, please?

40
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:06,583
Move!

41
00:02:07,875 --> 00:02:09,125
What the hell are you doing?

42
00:02:12,916 --> 00:02:13,833
Oh, Mr. Zhu.

43
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:15,458
Everything you asked for is ready.

44
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:16,875
Did you bring the materials?

45
00:02:16,875 --> 00:02:18,333
Don't worry. I've got everything.

46
00:02:18,416 --> 00:02:20,208
Good. Wait for me outside the office.

47
00:02:22,708 --> 00:02:24,833
Fuck. Working weekends again.

48
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:26,625
Let's go.

49
00:02:30,458 --> 00:02:31,250
Come in.

50
00:02:32,458 --> 00:02:33,250
Mr. Wang.

51
00:02:33,416 --> 00:02:34,583
Sorry to bother you on the weekend.

52
00:02:35,041 --> 00:02:35,916
How's it coming along?

53
00:02:37,416 --> 00:02:39,625
The AI Running Assistant's main features
work.

54
00:02:39,708 --> 00:02:40,875
One more round of testing,

55
00:02:40,875 --> 00:02:42,000
and we should be ready to release it.

56
00:02:43,125 --> 00:02:44,250
As for user testing...

57
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:45,083
All right, I understand.

58
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:47,500
Can you finish it?

59
00:02:47,666 --> 00:02:48,458
Yes.

60
00:02:48,625 --> 00:02:50,208
Good. Leave the files here.

61
00:02:50,708 --> 00:02:52,250
Zhu, stay a moment.

62
00:02:58,833 --> 00:03:00,791
There'll be some personnel changes in late
September.

63
00:03:01,416 --> 00:03:02,708
The product director position is opening up.

64
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:03,708
Have you heard?

65
00:03:04,791 --> 00:03:05,708
A little.

66
00:03:06,416 --> 00:03:08,500
The boss has been watching your team lately.

67
00:03:08,916 --> 00:03:09,791
You've got something promising.

68
00:03:09,791 --> 00:03:10,875
It just needs one final push.

69
00:03:11,208 --> 00:03:12,375
It's a horse race now.

70
00:03:12,416 --> 00:03:13,625
Whichever team moves fastest

71
00:03:13,625 --> 00:03:14,375
gets the prize.

72
00:03:14,375 --> 00:03:15,541
You mean a full launch?

73
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:16,750
Don't get hung up on the wording.

74
00:03:16,750 --> 00:03:18,000
Just make sure the boss sees it.

75
00:03:22,791 --> 00:03:25,083
Mr. Wang, I've been a fast runner since I
was a kid.

76
00:04:08,208 --> 00:04:09,541
This project's really pushing everyone.

77
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:11,250
You've just joined us. Settling in okay?

78
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,833
It's fine. The AI runs alongside the users,

79
00:04:13,833 --> 00:04:15,375
and we run alongside the project.

80
00:04:16,458 --> 00:04:18,458
But with so many areas of AI,

81
00:04:18,458 --> 00:04:20,041
why did you choose a running app?

82
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:22,041
It doesn't sound all that new.

83
00:04:23,208 --> 00:04:24,375
Running is simple.

84
00:04:24,416 --> 00:04:25,500
Fast is fast.

85
00:04:25,708 --> 00:04:27,041
The numbers don't lie.

86
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,375
I want to come first.

87
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:32,375
First place sounds too aggressive.

88
00:04:32,791 --> 00:04:33,833
Let's settle for second.

89
00:04:33,875 --> 00:04:34,958
The tallest tree catches the wind.

90
00:04:37,791 --> 00:04:39,208
You've been working hard lately.

91
00:04:40,416 --> 00:04:42,000
What job isn't hard?

92
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:44,708
I overheard your talk with the boss that
day.

93
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:46,500
The company really values this project.

94
00:04:46,625 --> 00:04:48,500
One more push could get you promoted.

95
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:50,958
You're the one who deserves the credit.

96
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:53,000
Why do you push yourself so hard?

97
00:04:53,875 --> 00:04:54,791
For the money.

98
00:04:57,708 --> 00:04:58,583
What else?

99
00:04:59,875 --> 00:05:00,791
That's it.

100
00:05:04,833 --> 00:05:06,583
No traumatic family backstory?

101
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:08,083
A gambling father,

102
00:05:08,208 --> 00:05:09,208
a sick mother,

103
00:05:09,291 --> 00:05:10,041
a younger brother still in school,

104
00:05:10,041 --> 00:05:11,250
and you, broken by it all?

105
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:13,875
What's wrong with you?

106
00:05:18,416 --> 00:05:19,375
My name is Zhu Tong.

107
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:21,375
I'm a product manager at a small company.

108
00:05:21,708 --> 00:05:25,000
Ever since I was little, I competed in
everything: grades, sports.

109
00:05:25,041 --> 00:05:26,208
Later, it was work.

110
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,166
But I always seemed to fall just short.

111
00:05:28,416 --> 00:05:29,416
Never first in class.

112
00:05:29,416 --> 00:05:30,583
Always second on the track.

113
00:05:30,625 --> 00:05:32,875
Even as an adult, someone was always ahead
of me.

114
00:05:33,291 --> 00:05:34,583
Maybe I was short on luck,

115
00:05:34,666 --> 00:05:35,583
or short on ability.

116
00:05:35,583 --> 00:05:37,375
Or maybe my chance just hadn't come.

117
00:05:37,791 --> 00:05:38,833
After graduating from college,

118
00:05:38,833 --> 00:05:40,291
I joined a small company.

119
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,833
Over the years, I came close to first a few
times.

120
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:44,250
Every time, I fell just short.

121
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:46,291
But at work, there's no medal for second
place.

122
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,083
The Running Assistant was the first project
I led.

123
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:50,583
And for the first time, I felt

124
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:53,041
that position was finally within reach.

125
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,416
September 30.

126
00:05:54,833 --> 00:05:56,958
This time, I was sure.

127
00:05:57,583 --> 00:05:58,166
I wanted to win.

128
00:06:01,166 --> 00:06:01,958
Did you hear?

129
00:06:02,083 --> 00:06:03,625
Xiao Wu from the other team got laid off.

130
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:04,958
She got laid off?

131
00:06:05,416 --> 00:06:06,708
But she worked so hard.

132
00:06:06,875 --> 00:06:09,041
God of Wealth, grant me my N-plus-one
severance.

133
00:06:40,541 --> 00:06:43,583
Next, the AI business and personnel changes.

134
00:06:45,458 --> 00:06:48,041
Several of our projects have made good
progress.

135
00:06:48,750 --> 00:06:50,458
To support commercialization,

136
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:52,833
the company will launch an AI Health
Assistant

137
00:06:53,458 --> 00:06:54,958
within the Smart Sports Products Department.

138
00:06:55,625 --> 00:06:57,375
The existing project teams will be
reassigned.

139
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,250
Following management's decision,

140
00:06:59,791 --> 00:07:02,125
Li Ming is promoted to product director

141
00:07:02,458 --> 00:07:05,000
to lead the new department and its projects.

142
00:07:17,875 --> 00:07:20,041
Thank you for your trust and support.

143
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:22,458
For running training, we've developed

144
00:07:22,458 --> 00:07:24,541
personalized training plans, motion
recognition,

145
00:07:24,541 --> 00:07:26,791
and real-time running companionship.

146
00:07:27,041 --> 00:07:29,083
The entire workflow is now operational.

147
00:07:29,291 --> 00:07:31,333
In the next phase, we'll focus on

148
00:07:31,333 --> 00:07:33,750
optimizing training data and
commercialization,

149
00:07:33,958 --> 00:07:35,625
with a view to launching soon.

150
00:07:39,208 --> 00:07:40,000
What's going on?

151
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,041
I developed all the features in Li Ming's
project.

152
00:07:42,041 --> 00:07:43,666
How did he get the promotion?

153
00:07:44,625 --> 00:07:45,875
I don't know the details.

154
00:07:46,208 --> 00:07:47,375
The boss decided on the promotion.

155
00:07:47,375 --> 00:07:48,541
It's not up to me.

156
00:07:48,875 --> 00:07:50,541
I've seen how hard you've worked.

157
00:07:50,541 --> 00:07:52,000
I'm sure there'll be another chance.

158
00:07:52,041 --> 00:07:52,750
But...

159
00:07:52,750 --> 00:07:53,833
Oh, it's raining.

160
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,708
Here's to a bright future!

161
00:07:58,166 --> 00:07:59,250
Congratulations, Director Li.

162
00:07:59,291 --> 00:08:00,083
Thank you.

163
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:31,750
Why?

164
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,208
Why?

165
00:08:33,750 --> 00:08:35,250
I did all the work.

166
00:08:36,125 --> 00:08:37,458
Why has it happened again?

167
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:41,166
Why do I always fall just short?

168
00:08:57,541 --> 00:08:58,791
Could Zhu Tong's family come here, please?

169
00:08:58,791 --> 00:09:00,208
The results are back.

170
00:09:00,625 --> 00:09:02,291
His condition is not looking good.

171
00:09:02,666 --> 00:09:03,916
He may only have a day or two left.

172
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:04,916
You should prepare yourselves.

173
00:09:27,875 --> 00:09:28,791
Grandpa, what's wrong?

174
00:09:29,541 --> 00:09:30,375
Young man,

175
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,875
I'd like to go a little further.

176
00:09:32,875 --> 00:09:34,625
Could you push me over there?

177
00:09:34,750 --> 00:09:35,916
I'll get a nurse.

178
00:09:36,125 --> 00:09:37,166
They're very busy.

179
00:09:37,291 --> 00:09:38,208
Let's not bother them.

180
00:09:38,958 --> 00:09:41,208
Just unlock the brakes on my wheels.

181
00:09:41,375 --> 00:09:42,416
We'll be there in no time.

182
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,375
This rain never lets up.

183
00:09:46,583 --> 00:09:48,708
I know. The laundry won't dry.

184
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:50,708
Wait!

185
00:09:58,791 --> 00:09:59,750
Oh no!

186
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:00,791
Something's happened!

187
00:10:06,791 --> 00:10:08,250
Am I already dead?

188
00:10:19,458 --> 00:10:20,250
Grandpa!

189
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:26,333
Grandpa, are you all right?

190
00:10:26,375 --> 00:10:27,916
Those people back there keep calling you.

191
00:10:28,041 --> 00:10:29,500
Why are you running so fast?

192
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:33,708
I can't catch up with you, Zhu Tong.

193
00:10:36,208 --> 00:10:38,000
Your voice sounds so familiar.

194
00:10:38,541 --> 00:10:40,416
Am I going senile?

195
00:10:41,125 --> 00:10:42,208
That day after school,

196
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:43,791
why didn't you come with us?

197
00:10:43,791 --> 00:10:45,833
Didn't we agree to have cake together?

198
00:10:46,250 --> 00:10:48,541
I ate so much I got a stomachache.

199
00:10:51,416 --> 00:10:52,208
Thank you.

200
00:10:53,250 --> 00:10:54,416
Thank you, all of you.

201
00:10:54,791 --> 00:10:57,416
But I'm used to being alone now.

202
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:58,666
You're not alone.

203
00:10:58,708 --> 00:10:59,833
I'm just like you.

204
00:11:00,583 --> 00:11:02,041
Someone who got left behind?

205
00:11:02,333 --> 00:11:03,583
Yeah. That's right.

206
00:11:04,041 --> 00:11:06,833
Looks like I never made it big after all.

207
00:11:07,583 --> 00:11:10,333
I'm sorry. There's no road ahead.

208
00:11:10,333 --> 00:11:11,625
This is as far as we go.

209
00:11:12,375 --> 00:11:15,291
Is it over when the doctors and my family
catch up?

210
00:11:17,916 --> 00:11:19,916
How should I finish?

211
00:11:20,458 --> 00:11:22,041
The way a runner-up would.

212
00:11:22,083 --> 00:11:23,458
You still have one spectator.

213
00:11:23,458 --> 00:11:24,458
Show him.

214
00:11:26,166 --> 00:11:28,750
What's your name, young man?

215
00:11:30,416 --> 00:11:32,375
My name is Hu Zhixiang.

216
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,250
When I was your age,

217
00:11:35,458 --> 00:11:36,958
I took part in a school sports day.

218
00:11:37,208 --> 00:11:38,583
I thought it was a sprint.

219
00:11:39,458 --> 00:11:41,083
Turns out it was a marathon.

220
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:42,625
Now,

221
00:11:43,125 --> 00:11:44,125
it's finally over.

222
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:45,625
Zhixiang,

223
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:46,916
watch closely.
